# The corpus is the source of truth and is deliberately not committed.
# See AGENTS.md section 1.4.
#
# Anchored to the repo root with a leading slash. A bare `corpus/` also matches
# src/laya_pipeline/corpus/, which is the discovery/markdown/models *package* —
# ignoring it would silently drop 750 lines of source from the repository.
/corpus/

# Every generated artifact: chunks, questions, negatives, labels, datasets,
# checkpoints and evaluation reports may embed derived corpus text.
# Also root-anchored, for the same reason: a bare `outputs/` or `data/` would
# match a directory of that name inside a package or a test fixture.
/outputs/
/data/
*.jsonl
!tests/fixtures/**/*.jsonl

# Environment and secrets. Endpoints and model names belong in the config file;
# anything genuinely local and secret belongs here.
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/